WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.570
October 1973. Arab oil producers
begin an embargo on oil exports.

2
00:00:06.570 --> 00:00:10.310
By January 1974, a
barrel of oil costs about

3
00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:16.290
four times as much: from
2.90 dollars to 11.65.

4
00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:18.690
Usually, when the price level rises,

5
00:00:18.690 --> 00:00:21.040
firms are keen to produce more.

6
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.480
In the United States, prices
rose fast while output fell.

7
00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.120
Economists called it stagflation.

8
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.950
So how can one shock
make an economy produce

9
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:34.330
less and charge more, both at once?

10
00:00:34.330 --> 00:00:37.350
In this mission, you'll see
why firms usually supply

11
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.720
more when the price level rises.

12
00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:41.900
Then you'll run a graph lab and watch what

13
00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:44.630
one shock does to the whole economy.

14
00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.820
Your mission: explain how
a single shock can bring

15
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.990
rising prices and falling output together.
